                    "response_metadata": {},
                    "type": "system",
                    "name": null,
                    "id": null
                  },
                  {
                    "content": "You are the Article Explainer service. A user has sent the following message:\n\n\"Here is an article about transformer attention mechanisms:\n\n[Article text: 'Attention mechanisms allow models to focus on relevant parts of the input. Multi-head attention uses several parallel attention heads. Each head learns different relationships. The outputs are concatenated and projected. This improves representational capacity. However, training can be unstable without proper initialization and regularization.']\n\nPlease provide a summary, an analogy for multi-head attention, and a short code sketch illustrating the concatenation step.\"\n\nProcess this request using the available specialists. Delegate the summary, analogy, and code illustration subtasks as appropriate. If you detect a deadlock in the wait-for graph among specialists, recover safely by selecting a victim and resolving the deadlock. Then produce one final structured answer that addresses all three requested facets.",
